@startuml seq_boot_programming
title SC-BOOT-01 - Nominal programming, steps 1 .. 19 (page 1 of 3: application and hand-over)

participant "UDS tester" as Tester
participant "Plant model" as Plant
box "TCU"
participant "Application" as App
participant "PBL" as PBL
participant "SBL" as SBL
end box

note over Tester, SBL
Covers: SYS-BOOT-001, SYS-BOOT-004, SYS-BOOT-005, SYS-BOOT-006, SYS-BOOT-008, SYS-BOOT-010, SYS-BOOT-011, SYS-BOOT-015,
SYS-BOOT-014, SYS-DIA-001, SYS-DIA-002, SYS-DIA-004, SYS-DIA-005, SYS-COM-005, SYS-STA-001,
SIM-TST-001, SIM-TST-004, SIM-GW-002, SIM-PLT-004
Sequence of reprogramming section 2. UDS requests on DIAG_PhysReq 0x7E1, responses on DIAG_Resp 0x7E9;
3E 80 on DIAG_FuncReq 0x7DF every 2 s during the whole sequence, no response (reprogramming section 2, can_matrix section 5).
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04; gateway <= 2 ms per direction (SIM-GW-002).
end note

note over App: control active, vehicle at standstill, selector P, speed valid;\nthe plant model keeps running on the same can0 (SIM-TST-004)

== Application: preconditions (steps 1 .. 4) ==
Tester -> App : [1] 10 03
App --> Tester : 50 03 00 32 01 F4
Tester -> App : [2] 31 01 02 03
App --> Tester : 71 01 02 03 00
note right: checkProgrammingPreconditions OK:\nstandstill, P, speed valid (SYS-DIA-004)
Tester -> App : [3] 85 02
App --> Tester : C5 02
Tester -> App : [4] 28 01 01
App --> Tester : 68 01
App -> App : stop TCU_Actuators / TCU_Status, reception continues (SYS-COM-005)
Plant -> Plant : no TCU_Actuators for 50 ms: hydraulic default (SIM-PLT-004)
Tester -> App : 3E 80 (0x7DF, every 2 s)

== Hand-over application -> PBL (step 5) ==
Tester -> App : [5] 10 02
App -> App : SYS-DIA-004 holds: accept
App --> Tester : 50 02 00 32 01 F4
note right of Tester: t5 = start of the programming time (SYS-BOOT-010)
App -> App : no response to any request until the reset;\nsoftware reset <= 20 ms after the response (SYS-BOOT-014)
loop every 5 ms until the PBL answers (reprogramming section 9)
  Tester -> PBL : 10 02
end
note over App, PBL: reset; no programming request is stored across the reset (SYS-BOOT-014)
PBL -> PBL : application check valid (SYS-BOOT-001); boot window 50 ms (SYS-BOOT-011)
PBL -> PBL : 10 02 received within the 50 ms window
PBL --> Tester : 50 02 00 32 01 F4
note right of PBL: PBL programming session;\nno TCU_Actuators / TCU_Status (SYS-BOOT-008)

newpage SC-BOOT-01 - Nominal programming (page 2 of 3: PBL programming session, steps 6 .. 11)

== PBL: security access and SBL download (steps 6 .. 10) ==
Tester -> PBL : [6] 27 11
PBL --> Tester : 67 11 <seed, 4 bytes>
Tester -> PBL : 27 12 <key = rotl32(seed, 7) XOR 0x5A3C_C3A5>
PBL --> Tester : 67 12
note right of PBL: level 0x11 unlocked (SYS-BOOT-005)
Tester -> PBL : [7] 34 00 44 04 00 00 00 <memSize>
PBL -> PBL : range inside the SBL load area 0x0400_0000 .. 0x0400_FFFF (reprogramming section 11.1)
PBL --> Tester : 74 20 04 02
note right of PBL: maxNumberOfBlockLength 0x0402 = 1024 data bytes\n+ SID + block sequence counter (reprogramming section 12)
loop [8] for each block of the SBL image
  Tester -> PBL : 36 <bsc> <up to 1024 data bytes>
  PBL -> PBL : write the block into SRAMX (no flash access, SYS-BOOT-004)
  PBL --> Tester : 76 <bsc>
end
Tester -> PBL : [9] 37
PBL --> Tester : 77
Tester -> PBL : [10] 31 01 02 02 <crc32 of the SBL image>
PBL --> Tester : 71 01 02 02 00
note right of PBL: checkMemory of the SBL: CRC-32/ISO-HDLC OK
Tester -> PBL : 3E 80 (0x7DF, every 2 s)

== PBL -> SBL: activation (step 11) ==
Tester -> PBL : [11] 31 01 03 01
PBL -> PBL : last 0202 returned 0 and the SBL header is valid\n(magic 0x53544178 xATS, header_crc32) (reprogramming section 11.1)
PBL -> SBL : start the SBL in SRAMX; hand over programming session,\nsecurity unlocked and CAN configuration in RAM (reprogramming section 1)
SBL --> Tester : 71 01 03 01 00
note right of SBL: answered by the SBL; no new 27 needed

newpage SC-BOOT-01 - Nominal programming (page 3 of 3: SBL programming session, steps 12 .. 19, restart)

== SBL: fingerprint, erase, application download (steps 12 .. 16) ==
Tester -> SBL : [12] 2E F1 5A <fingerprint, 16 bytes>
SBL -> SBL : write the boot info slot that is not the newest: fingerprint,\nprogramming counter (DID FD00) + 1, sequence + 1 (reprogramming section 7)
SBL --> Tester : 6E F1 5A
Tester -> SBL : [13] 31 01 FF 00 44 00 01 40 00 <memSize>
SBL -> SBL : range inside the application area 0x0001_4000 .. 0x000F_FFFF,\nsector-aligned (8 KiB) (SYS-BOOT-006); runs only from RAM (RB-04)
loop while the erase is busy
  SBL --> Tester : 7F 31 78
  note right of SBL: responsePending at least every\nP2* - 500 ms = 4500 ms (RB-05)
end
SBL --> Tester : 71 01 FF 00 00
Tester -> SBL : [14] 34 00 44 00 01 40 00 <memSize>
SBL --> Tester : 74 20 04 02
loop [15] for each block of the application image (1 KiB header first)
  Tester -> SBL : 36 <bsc> <up to 1024 data bytes>
  SBL -> SBL : program flash in 16-byte phrases (only the SBL erases / writes flash,\nSYS-BOOT-004); last block padded with 0xFF by the tester
  SBL --> Tester : 76 <bsc>
end
Tester -> SBL : [16] 37
SBL --> Tester : 77
Tester -> SBL : 3E 80 (0x7DF, every 2 s)

== SBL: checks and reset (steps 17 .. 19) ==
Tester -> SBL : [17] 31 01 02 02 <crc32 of the application image>
SBL -> SBL : clear the flash cache, disable speculation (RB-03); CRC OK
SBL --> Tester : 71 01 02 02 00
Tester -> SBL : [18] 31 01 FF 01
SBL -> SBL : header valid, hw_id 0x0947_0001,\nmin_pbl_version <= PBL version (reprogramming section 11)
SBL -> SBL : program the application header sector 0x0001_4000 .. 0x0001_5FFF last,\nafter 0202 and FF01 passed (SYS-BOOT-015)
SBL --> Tester : 71 01 FF 01 00
Tester -> SBL : [19] 11 01
SBL --> Tester : 51 01
note right of Tester: end of 11 01: programming time from t5\n<= 60 s for a 256 KiB application (SYS-BOOT-010)
note over PBL, SBL: reset: the SBL in RAM and the unlocked security state are discarded

== restart ==
PBL -> PBL : application check valid (SYS-BOOT-001); 50 ms boot window without 10 02
PBL -> App : jump to the application
App -> Plant : TCU_Actuators every 10 ms, TCU_Status every 100 ms
note right of App: control active <= 500 ms after the reset (SYS-STA-001), see SC-STA-01
Tester -> App : 22 F1 81
App --> Tester : 62 F1 81 <new sw_version>
Tester -> Tester : show the result; stop with a clear message on any negative\nresponse or timeout (SIM-TST-001)
@enduml
